    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **263 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership level is computed in `OwnerMapper.java` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`), a MapStruct expression. Previously it was:\n\n```java\nMath.min(3, 1 + <email factor> + <namesake factor>)\n```\n\nI raised the cap to 4 and added a tenure factor that grants the extra level only when tenure exceeds 365 days:\n\n```java\nMath.min(4, 1\n    + (email present ? 1 : 0)\n    + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0)\n    + (registrationDate != null\n        && ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365 ? 1 : 0))\n```\n\nTenure is measured from the owner's `registrationDate` (set to the current business day for a new owner). Since a newly created owner has zero tenure, the tenure factor contributes 0, so a new owner with an email and a `namesakeCount` of 0 lands at exactly level 3 (`1 + 1 + 1`) and can never reach level 4 \u2014 matching the spec. Only owners whose registration is more than 365 days in the past can reach level 4.",
